invariant: INV-51
file: src/sha512_avx2.c
catches: test/lint-schedule-order.sh
reason: one_round adds T1 and Maj first and Sigma0 last. Every digest is
  the same. clang 23 then writes all 145 vector instructions of the loop
  of sixteen rounds after its last round, and SHA-384 over 16 KiB took
  1.28 times as long on an EPYC 7763 (docs/decisions.md 230). No two
  vector instructions of the loop then have a long run between them: the
  long run is the one from the loop's last vector instruction to its
  first one in the next pass. make lint-schedule-order counts that run
  and requires at most 40.

--- old
    *h = t1 + (upper_sigma0(a) + majority(a, b, c));
--- new
    *h = (t1 + majority(a, b, c)) + upper_sigma0(a);
